Fillets: the corner of a contour closed by a sharp corner, at a vertex with
more than three sharp edges (mitcad#122).

A chain of tangent edges that closes on itself at a vertex where its first
and last edges meet at an angle gives one stripe with both ends at that
vertex; the vertex lists the stripe twice. ChFi3d_Builder::PerformTwoCorner
handles that (the second occurrence is the last end), but
PerformMoreThreeCorner, which takes such vertices when they hold more than
three sharp edges, matched the edges around the vertex against the first
end of each stripe only (ChFi3d_IndexOfSurfData). The last edge of the
contour was taken for an edge without a fillet, the stripe's last end got
no corner curve and no points, and ChFi3d_FilDS then added point
interferences with index 0 (Standard_ProgramError
"TopOpeBRepDS_DataStructure::Point" in ChFi3d_Builder::Compute). The edge
parsing now also matches the last end of a stripe whose last edge ends at
the vertex, and the indices of the surface data come from the end recorded
for each edge.
